Title: 0010-big-endian-hosts
Repository: micropoliscore
Base-Commit: 69ccf87ed72d2d2950b70cf16ef1391439bd9d48
Requires: 0009-free-sprite-lists.patch
Author: AmigaOS 3.x port
Date: 2026-11-05
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: generic - big-endian hosts whose compiler does not define __BIG_ENDIAN__

Problem:
  fileio.cpp chooses the word swap with #if !defined(__BIG_ENDIAN__). GCC for m68k (AmigaOS 3.x) does not define __BIG_ENDIAN__, so the big-endian 68k host swapped the big-endian .cty words and every city loaded and saved byte-swapped.
Solution:
  Decide on __BYTE_ORDER__ == __ORDER_BIG_ENDIAN__ (defined by GCC and Clang on every target), falling back to __BIG_ENDIAN__, else little-endian.
Validation:
  cross-compiled for m68k-amigaos; to be checked by loading the bundled cities on the Amiga.
Removal:
  Permanent fix.

diff --git a/packages/micropolis-engine/src/fileio.cpp b/packages/micropolis-engine/src/fileio.cpp
index 10d0345..e121ced 100644
--- a/packages/micropolis-engine/src/fileio.cpp
+++ b/packages/micropolis-engine/src/fileio.cpp
@@ -99,7 +99,19 @@
  */
 
 
-#if !defined(__BIG_ENDIAN__)
+/* GCC and Clang name the byte order in __BYTE_ORDER__ on every target;
+ * __BIG_ENDIAN__ is only defined on some (PowerPC, not m68k), so a
+ * big-endian 68k host would otherwise swap words that are already in
+ * file order and load every classic city as garbage. */
+#if defined(__BYTE_ORDER__) && defined(__ORDER_BIG_ENDIAN__)
+#define MICROPOLIS_HOST_BIG_ENDIAN (__BYTE_ORDER__ == __ORDER_BIG_ENDIAN__)
+#elif defined(__BIG_ENDIAN__)
+#define MICROPOLIS_HOST_BIG_ENDIAN 1
+#else
+#define MICROPOLIS_HOST_BIG_ENDIAN 0
+#endif
+
+#if !MICROPOLIS_HOST_BIG_ENDIAN
 
